  <!-- </section> -->
  <div class="container">
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-2">

        <!-- Title -->
        <h6 class="title">
          Quentin Donaldson
        </h6>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-10">
        <!-- Text -->
        <p class="text-muted mb-5">
          Having completed his two honours degrees at the University of Cape Town, Mr Donaldson went on to complete his
          articles under the direct mentorship of William Booth (who acted as the Chairperson of the Criminal Law
          Society
          at the time and ran what is widely regarded as the top criminal law firm in Cape Town). Having thereafter run
          his own law firm for some time in Cape Town, Mr Donaldson accepted a corporate position in Johannesburg as a
          national litigation manager, before joining the Bar as an Advocate where he practiced primarily in Commercial
          and Labour Law. Thereafter, Adv Donaldson (as he was then) went on to head up The Labour Counsel as its
          Managing
          Director. Having done this for approximately five years, Adv. Donaldson converted back to being an attorney
          and
          immediately opened Donaldson Attorneys Incorporated which has seen exceptional growth based on its success
          rate
          and client relationships.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-2">

        <!-- Title -->
        <h6 class="title">
          Michelle Lage
        </h6>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-10">
        <!-- Text -->
        <p class="text-muted mb-5">
          Ms. Lage holds an LLB and Masters' Degree in Commercial Law and has since gained extensive experience in
          various practice areas including labour, litigation. Upholding the firm's values consistently demonstrating
          exceptional client service, Ms. Lage was promoted to a Senior Associate relatively quickly. Whilst managing a
          substantial workload, Ms Lage still dedicates a significant amount of time to staff training and helps the
          firm to ensure that the right results are consistently achieved.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-2">

        <!-- Title -->
        <h6 class="title">
          Gugu Mbalati
        </h6>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-10">
        <!-- Text -->
        <p class="text-muted mb-5">
          Ms G. Mbalati is a practising Attorney with expertise in labour law. She provides strategic and authoritative
          guidance on a wide range of employment and labour-related matters, drawing on her experience in Industrial
          Relations and Labour Law consultancy. Ms Mbalati possesses a well-established and comprehensive understanding
          of collective bargaining, dispute resolution, workplace policy development, and proceedings before the
          Commission for Conciliation, Mediation and Arbitration (CCMA).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <div class="col-md-2">

        <!-- Title -->
        <h6 class="title">
          Resego Dibakwane
        </h6>
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-10">
        <!-- Text -->
        <p class="text-muted mb-5">
          Ms. R Dibakwane obtained her LLB degree from the University of Johannesburg and has vast experience in
          commercial and corporate law. Ms. Dibakwane has developed a keen interest in Labour Law and has chaired dozens
          of hearings and excels in achieving voluntary termination outcomes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

